{"seq":4,"id":"NT1","type":"note","at":"2026-11-14T19:50:39Z","by":"AC1","prev":"sha256:e54845c36b1da160a22e91cff4f318c67b59ab75b8bc7e8089ba174ad7d83569","content_hash":"sha256:fd1413e1792d9ce89fb8bbe8fbcd901a860501f37e3c9278661127afcae31edf","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"text":"Brief requirements (the supervisor, 2026-11-14): (1) a study separate from the review entrylib:2026.000008, supporting its claims; (2) simulations with simple models; (3) the measures MAE, RMSE, MAPE and sMAPE; (4) what each measure recommends: the point forecast or method it selects; (5) a variety of situations; (6) a plan and hypotheses, recorded with claimset lab. The script lines that meet each are listed once the script exists."}}
{"seq":5,"id":"Q1","type":"question","at":"2026-11-14T19:50:41Z","by":"AC1","prev":"sha256:af85fc02033eb8e87efa1407e430d0392a0859d722f6f63cb5e754bfe2ca1b45","content_hash":"sha256:019971f65498d2783cac12a777567fe3af0f15df208a795ce44d7f2acff901ac","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"text":"Which point forecasts and which forecasting methods do RMSE, MAE, MAPE and sMAPE select when outcomes are symmetric, skewed or intermittent, and when series differ in scale, and do their choices agree with the claims of the review entrylib:2026.000008@v2?"}}
